            ("What are the three most common Indicator of Compromise (IoC) types?", ["File Hashes (SHA-256), IP Addresses, and Malicious Domain Names / URLs", "Usernames, Passwords, and First Names", "HTML tags, CSS classes, and JS functions", "Server model, CPU speed, and RAM size"], "File Hashes (SHA-256), IP Addresses, and Malicious Domain Names / URLs", "Hashes de fichiers, adresses IP et noms de domaine malveillants."),
            ("Complete: 'MITRE ___ provides a global knowledge base of adversary tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs).'", ["ATT&CK", "DEFENSE", "SHIELD", "MATRIX"], "ATT&CK", "MITRE ATT&CK."),
            ("What is 'Fileless Malware'?", ["Malicious code that operates entirely in memory (RAM) or abuses legitimate system binaries (LOLBins) without dropping executable files to disk", "Malware written in plain text", "Malware sent by postal mail", "A hardware keyboard bug"], "Malicious code that operates entirely in memory (RAM) or abuses legitimate system binaries (LOLBins) without dropping executable files to disk", "Code malveillant résidant en RAM ou détournant des binaires légitimes (Living Off the Land).")
